{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>You shall observe, to offer to Me.</b> Just as the observance stated regarding the Passover is by inspection, so too the observance stated here is by inspection." "<b>To offer to Me at its appointed time.</b> Even on the Sabbath, even in impurity — if no pure person is found, he does not neglect its offering — and even at a time of war. And so we find with Joshua, that the angel rebuked him for having suspended the daily offering when they besieged Jericho. Another interpretation: <b>at its appointed time</b> — that they not offer it too early before morning nor delay it after evening."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:00.243824065Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}